  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Postal Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this proposal is to demonstrate measurable changes in human access and wildlife population numbers, particularly ungulates, resulting from logging road closures in order to prove the effectiveness of closures for tiger conservation. This would be done by: (a) closing unused logging roads; (b) measuring changes in wildlife populations; (c) measuring changes in human use; (d) designing closures that facilitate effective law enforcement; and (e) promoting road closures as a necessary component of FSC certification...Specifically the applicant would select six roads within the Maksimovka River drainage and close three of these roads once the ground thaws in the spring 2013 and then (a) measure changes in wildlife populations; (2) measure changes in human use; (3) design closures that facilitate effective law enforcement; and (4) promote road closures as a necessary component of FSC certification.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
